### Lab 1: Students bucket — create/store, retrieve, update, delete
### Store a JSON student record
curl -i -X PUT http://127.0.0.1:8098/buckets/students/keys/S001 \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -d '{"name":"Aarav Sharma","course":"BCA","city":"Roorkee"}'

### Retrieve
curl -i http://127.0.0.1:8098/buckets/students/keys/S001

### Update (PUT replaces the stored value at the same key)
curl -i -X PUT http://127.0.0.1:8098/buckets/students/keys/S001 \
  -H 'Content-Type: application/json' \
  -d '{"name":"Aarav Sharma","course":"BCA","city":"Dehradun"}'

### Delete
curl -i -X DELETE http://127.0.0.1:8098/buckets/students/keys/S001
curl -i http://127.0.0.1:8098/buckets/students/keys/S001
